          "title": "You'll want to know: گرجنا",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "گرجنا — garajnā — \"to thunder; to roar\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "رات کو بادل گرج رہے تھے۔ rāt ko bādal garaj rahe the. The clouds were thundering in the night."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Past (it …): وہ شیر گرج اٹھا, voh sher garaj uṭhā."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "is inherited from Sanskrit gárjati, \"thunders, roars\", where CDIAL lists the Hindi cousin gājnā (CDIAL 4046); گرجنا (garajnā) keeps the Sanskrit shape closer. Clouds گرجتے ہیں, and so does a lion."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
